module v1.tests.claim.v1_annotation_target_emission_test


data v1_annotation_target_emission_offline_recipe: String = "OFFLINE LOCAL RECIPE: target/release/claim_batch --source-root dag --source-root src/v1 --entry src/v1/tests/claim/v1_annotation_target_emission_test.dag --functions w_the_annotated_source_still_produces_annotation_rows"

data v1_annotation_target_emission_note: String = "D-C property 4: the same program written with and without prose must produce the SAME EXECUTABLE OUTPUT. This is the end of the erasure chain — the other six controls compare parser-level facts, and this one compares the bytes a downstream toolchain actually compiles. It is the claim that would notice if a future change routed the authored graph into emission without deciding to, since ResolvedPipelineResult and emit_resolved_for_target do not carry that graph at all today and the erasure is therefore total by omission rather than by design.

THE THREE ARMS ARE ONE CLAIM, NOT THREE CONVENIENCES. Byte equality alone is satisfied by an emitter that returns the same thing for every input — including nothing at all — so the second arm requires the same rendering to DIFFER on a real semantic change, and the third requires the annotated source to have actually carried prose. Without arm two the equality is a tautology; without arm three it is an equality between two sources that may both have been comment-free.

ALL THREE ARMS HOLD. Arm three executes here, in this file, as an enrolled witness. Arms one and two were established by host execution rather than enrolled, and property_4_emission_measurement below records exactly what was run, what came back, and why enrollment is not available — read it before treating the split as a gap."

data annotated_source: String = "module emit_probe\n\n// prose about alpha\ndata alpha: Int = 1\n\n// prose about probe\nfn probe(x: Int) -> Int {\n  x + alpha\n}\n"

data bare_source: String = "module emit_probe\n\ndata alpha: Int = 1\n\nfn probe(x: Int) -> Int {\n  x + alpha\n}\n"

data property_4_emission_measurement: String = "ARMS ONE AND TWO, BY HOST EXECUTION. Three fixtures were emitted through the real compiler on 2026-08-05, each its own source root holding one module: the annotated twin, the bare twin, and a semantically changed twin whose only difference from the bare one is `data alpha: Int = 2` instead of `1`.

  target/release/gunbc compile --source-root <fixture> --output-dir <out> --target rust

Every fixture emitted six files at exit 0 with zero diagnostics — Cargo.toml, src/lib.rs, src/main.rs, src/emit_probe.rs, src/v1_rt.rs, src/v2_std_integer.rs. `diff -r` over the annotated and bare outputs reports NO DIFFERENCE: identical bytes in all six, so the prose reached the target program nowhere, not in a comment, not in a string, not in a length. The same `diff -r` over the bare and semantically changed outputs reports a difference, which is what stops the first comparison from being a statement about an emitter that ignores its input.

WHY THIS IS A RECEIPT AND NOT AN ENROLLED WITNESS. There is no .dag-reachable surface that returns emitted target BYTES. Measured, not assumed: compile_to_resolved called from interpreted .dag raises `type error: map_keys expects a map, got Record`, and the failure is in the RESOLVE half — emit_resolved_for_target is never reached — reproduced on the smallest possible input, one module containing `fn probe() -> Bool { true }`. It is not a property of the annotated fixture or of a missing pool, and it is a pre-existing model-versus-realization fork in load-bearing v1 machinery that M1A has no business repairing.

WHY NO PROXY AND NO NEW BUILTIN. The two host arms that do work return a Bool and a diagnostic census; neither carries bytes. Asserting through the Bool that `both twins compile successfully` would wear this property's name and prove almost nothing, passing for any pair of compiling programs whatever they emit — the fail-open proxy oracle DESIGN forbids. Adding a third bytes-returning arm would grow hand-maintained cli_run.rs to satisfy a witness, against the hollowing plan that seed is tracked by, and that is a decision for the emitter lane rather than a side effect of this one.

NEXT TRIGGER: a .dag-reachable surface returning emitted files for a synthetic source — compile_to_resolved executing under the interpreter, or an emitter-lane host arm that carries bytes. Then all three arms enroll together in this file and this receipt dissolves."

fn annotation_row_count(source: String) -> Int {
  let artifact = tokenize_artifact(source: source, file: "emit_probe.dag")
  let parsed = parse_with_table(
    tokens: artifact.tokens,
    source_indices: map_insert(empty_map(), "emit_probe.dag", build_newline_index(file: "emit_probe.dag", source: source)),
    intern_table: empty_intern_table(),
  )
  source_annotation_graph_rows(
    graph: annotation_attachment_result_graph(
      result: bind_annotations(
        transport: parsed.occurrence_transport,
        captures: artifact.annotations,
        source_length: string_length(s: source)
      )
    )
  ) |> count
}

test fn w_the_annotated_source_still_produces_annotation_rows() -> Bool {
  annotation_row_count(source: annotated_source) == 2 &&
    annotation_row_count(source: bare_source) == 0
}
